if there's anything you could say is a  true constant  in today's entertainment industry it's  this what the rock says  goes dwayne johnson's on-camera talents  and unshakable work ethic have turned  him into one of the biggest a-listers in  the world  in every sense of the word even though  hollywood's biggest name  has a few forgotten failures in his  resume the fact that johnson is able to  say that he's the wealthiest star in the  entire fast and furious franchise  more than makes up for the occasional  turkey and he wasn't even  part of the original squad thanks to  johnson's borderline superhuman  achievements in the movie business  and his impressive physique of course  fans have long been clamoring to see him  kick things up a notch and play an  actual superhero or as the case may be  super villain and sure enough johnson  has lately been getting the most ripped  he's ever been  in order to play black adam the  dangerous predecessor turned  nemesis of the superhero shazam and he's  not just showing up in a few scenes in  someone else's feature either  oh no johnson's black adam is getting  his very own movie  the black adam solo film has been in  development for a good while now  so it's been easy to assume that the  movie has been chugging along at  whatever pace  warner brothers and dc entertainment can  manage but it looks like that pace is  rapidly quickening  as the rock has just revealed something  big the first pages of the black adam  script  in a three-minute video clip on  instagram johnson showed his 225 million  plus followers his copy of the black  adam script  written by adam stekiel with fresh  revisions courtesy of the mauritanian  writers rory haynes  and saurabh noshovani regarding the  movie's impending shooting dates  johnson had this to say i mean i can't  believe we are at the finish line  uh with this thing and what a journey it  has been that journey  johnson is referencing has been a rocky  one indeed  as it seems to reference the fact that  black adam was supposed to debut  in theaters in december of this year  before it was pulled off the schedule  indefinitely due to the coronavirus  pandemic  so it feels good to be on the verge of  bringing black adam to life johnson  continued to explain how he's been  fine-tuning the script over the last few  months  placing bright yellow stickers on pages  where he wanted to leave notes  as part of his intensive tequila fueled  script study  to celebrate the impending start of  filming johnson led his audience in on  this particular night of script study  lifting the veil by showing off the very  first page  which reads well i'd love to wear a  rainbow every day  and tell the world that everything's  okay but i'll try to carry off a little  darkness on my back  till things are brighter i'm the man in  black fans of country legend  johnny cash will no doubt recognize this  as a slightly modified  quote from his signature song man in  black and johnson stated that the quote  is instrumental to the very essence of  black adam  it gives you guys an example  of who black adam is and who black adam  is to the world of the dc  universe beyond that though johnson had  something to say about the movie's place  in the world of blockbuster superhero  movies and that is the dc universe  but that also includes the marvel  superhero universe too  realizing that this remark might have  broken the internet even further  johnson was good enough to clarify now  look i'm not saying that there's going  to be a mashup i'm not saying that but  what i am saying is it doesn't matter to  me and it doesn't matter it's a black  adam you put them all on notice  understandably this sneak peek has got  fans  very excited indeed so excited in fact  that a good portion of the post's  comments are simply  various combinations of thumbs up fire  and heart emojis  as well as heartfelt shows of support  for example  one user simply wrote hyped while  another commented  always are rock meanwhile one  appreciative cash fan simply said  johnny cash baby so yeah not a bad  response so far  and it seems like the rock fans and dc  fans alike are hugely enthusiastic to  finally see johnson play black adam  and since the actor also revealed that  he'll start shooting the movie in about  three weeks  which should be sometime in april it  looks like the day the movie finally  drops is inching closer and closer  until then keep an eye out for the man  in black folks  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

